Ido Yehieli <Ido.Yehieli@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> The question remains then, why does NetHack have relatively few
> variants?

There might be resp. have been more variants than you think. But, of
course nowhere as much as Angband has.

During my journey of snatching every valuable code from variants and
patches of NetHack, I made this little diagram (although by far not
complete, at least PatchHack and the biodiversity patch are missing):
http://sourceforge.net/apps/trac/unnethack/wiki/History


My personal theory is that people released less variants because
Slash'Em scooped up a lot of the good patches and if it's in Slash'Em
the patch has increased changes of getting into Vanilla. So there's
less incentive of releasing your own variant.


Somehow in the NetHack community it is enough to just publish the
patch in RGRN or on http://bilious.homelinux.org/

Do any of the other RL have a centralized patch repository?

